{
  "module": "Inference: prefill, decode and the cache",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "mqa-gqa",
    "title": "Multi-query and grouped-query attention",
    "summary": "Two ways of shrinking the KV cache by letting several query heads share one set of keys and values.",
    "covers": ["mqa-gqa"],
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "lesson": "kv-cache-size",
        "reason": "They exist to shrink that size."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "multi-head",
        "reason": "They change how heads share their K and V."
      }
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "the-problem",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The cache is large, and decode has to read all of it for every token. So it costs "
            },
            {
              "text": "memory",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", and it also costs "
            },
            {
              "text": "memory bandwidth",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ": the time spent reading it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Multi-query and grouped-query attention are designs that address exactly this: "
            },
            {
              "text": "the size and memory bandwidth of the KV cache during decoding",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 79, 76)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "standard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "In standard multi-head attention, every query head has "
            },
            {
              "text": "its own",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " K and V. The number of K/V heads equals the number of query heads, and that is the h_kv in the size formula."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 79, 78)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "mqa",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Multi-query attention (MQA)",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ": "
            },
            {
              "text": "all",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " the query heads share a "
            },
            {
              "text": "single",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " K/V head. There is one set of keys and values, and every query head reads it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 79)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "gqa",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Grouped-query attention (GQA)",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ": the query heads are divided into "
            },
            {
              "text": "groups",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": ", and each group shares "
            },
            {
              "text": "one",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " K/V head. It is a middle ground between standard multi-head attention (one K/V head per query head) and MQA (one for all)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 79)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "the-saving",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The cache shrinks by the ratio of query heads to K/V heads."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "A hypothetical, using the Llama-2-7B shape with 32 query heads:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "standard, 32 K/V heads: 0.5 MiB per token, 2 GiB at 4,096 tokens"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "GQA with 8 K/V heads: 0.125 MiB per token, 512 MiB at 4,096 tokens (4 times smaller)"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "MQA with 1 K/V head: 16 KiB per token, 64 MiB at 4,096 tokens (32 times smaller)"
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Llama 2 70B is an example of a model that uses GQA."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 79, 78)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "What problem do MQA and GQA address?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "correct": true,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The size and memory bandwidth of the KV cache during decoding"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "They make the cache smaller."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The number of tokens in the vocabulary"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The vocabulary is not involved."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The cost of training the tokenizer"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The tokenizer is built beforehand."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "correct": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The need for position information"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reason": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "That is solved by position schemes."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "teaches": ["the-problem"],
      "covers": ["mqa-gqa"],
      "variants": [
        {
          "prompt": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Why does a smaller KV cache help decoding speed as well as memory use?"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "options": [
            {
              "correct": true,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "Decode reads the whole cache for every token, so a smaller cache means less to read"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "Decode is limited by memory bandwidth."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "Because a smaller cache needs fewer layers"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "The number of layers is unchanged."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "Because it removes the need to read the weights"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "The weights are still read."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "correct": false,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "It does not: speed and memory are unrelated"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "reason": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "spans": [
                    {
                      "text": "Decode is limited by reading memory."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "What is multi-query attention (MQA)?"
